{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassGap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassGap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.TopologicalMass","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.BraneTower","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":48,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.confinement_glueball_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.confinement_glueball_pos","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L259-L262","doc":"Confinement implies the glueball mass is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.Confinement.glueball_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.Confinement.glueball_bound","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.Confinement.glueball_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.Confinement.glueball_mass","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.Confinement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.Confinement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L255-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.Confinement.toYangMillsMassGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.Confinement.toYangMillsMassGap","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L255-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.Confinement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.Confinement","kind":"structure","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L253-L257","doc":"**Confinement**: if the mass gap holds, then every finite-energy\nexcitation is a colour singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.yangMillsMassGap_construction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.yangMillsMassGap_construction","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L235-L249","doc":"**The millennium conjecture**: per-instance form derived from\n`HasYangMillsMassGap`. The deprecated universal axiom\n`yangMillsMassGap_construction` has been removed; callers must\nbind `[HasYangMillsMassGap q tm]` to obtain a witness for the\nspecific `(q, tm)` they care about.\n\nRef: [jaffe2006] https://www.claymath.org/millennium/yang-mills-the-maths-gap/\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 5, §1 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_tm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_tm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Implication: the witness uses the expected transfer matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_q_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_q_eq","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L231-L231","doc":"Implication: the witness has the expected substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.impl_witness","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L229-L229","doc":"Implication: a `YangMillsMassGap` instance exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.gap_present","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.gap_present","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L227-L227","doc":"Hypothesis that the mass gap holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.mass_gap_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.mass_gap_holds","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L225-L225","doc":"Proposition: the Yang-Mills mass gap holds for (q, tm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.HasYangMillsMassGap","kind":"class","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L214-L233","doc":"**Typeclass version of the Yang–Mills mass gap conjecture**.\n\nPattern 4 (typeclass conversion): instead of asserting existence\nfor all `q > 1`, callers instantiate this class for their specific\n`q` and transfer matrix. The `sorry` in instances is understood as\n**conjecture**, not missing proof (per AGENTS.md §3b).\n\nRef: [jaffe2006] https://www.claymath.org/millennium/yang-mills-the-maths-gap/\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 5, §1 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.yang_mills_gap_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.yang_mills_gap_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L209-L212","doc":"The gap is bounded below by the provable crossing-energy bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.yang_mills_gap_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.yang_mills_gap_positive","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L205-L207","doc":"In any `YangMillsMassGap` instance, the gap is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.gap_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.gap_positive","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L203-L203","doc":"**Positivity of gap**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.mass_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.mass_gap","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L201-L201","doc":"**Mass gap**: the first excited eigenvalue is bounded below\nby the minimum crossing energy times `(q − 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.transferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.transferMatrix","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L198-L198","doc":"The categorical transfer matrix (bundles its own dla + vacuum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.hq","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.q","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L194-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.YangMillsMassGap","kind":"structure","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L191-L203","doc":"**Conjecture (Yang–Mills existence and mass gap).**\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:yang-mills-mass-gap}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:yang-mills-mass-gap","label":"conj:yang-mills-mass-gap","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/yang-mills-mass-gap.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.twoPoint_gap_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.twoPoint_gap_positive","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L177-L187","doc":"If the transfer matrix has a mass gap, the gap value is positive.\n\nAUDIT NOTE: Previously named `twoPoint_exponential_decay`, which was\nmisleading — the theorem only restates gap positivity, not exponential\ndecay. The actual exponential decay bound `|G(t)| ≤ C·e^{-Δ₀·t}`\nrequires spectral theory not yet formalised. Renamed for honesty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.eval","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L175-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.coefficients_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.coefficients_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L174-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.coefficients","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.coefficients","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L173-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.tm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.tm","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L172-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwoPointFunction","kind":"structure","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L169-L175","doc":"The **categorical two-point function**: the Frobenius pairing\nof a vortex morphism with its time-translated copy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.gapValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.gapValue","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L162-L165","doc":"The mass gap value (first non-zero eigenvalue). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.hasMassGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.hasMassGap","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L157-L160","doc":"A transfer matrix has a **mass gap** if the first excited state\nhas strictly positive eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues_mono","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L155-L155","doc":"Eigenvalues are non-decreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Eigenvalues are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vacuum_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vacuum_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L151-L151","doc":"The vacuum eigenvalue is zero (by definition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.eigenvalues","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L149-L149","doc":"Eigenvalues of the transfer matrix, indexed by ℕ\n(ordered by increasing energy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vacuum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vacuum","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L146-L146","doc":"The vacuum state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.dla","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.dla","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L144-L144","doc":"The direct limit algebra (brane tower endomorphisms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix.mk","kind":"ctor","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L142-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix","kind":"structure","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L136-L155","doc":"The **categorical transfer matrix** on the endomorphism algebra\nat level `n` of the brane tower.  This is the categorical\nanalogue of the Hamiltonian: its spectrum determines the mass\nspectrum of excitations.\n\nLaTeX: referenced in `\\label{def:categorical-transfer-matrix}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_mono","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L92-L132","doc":"The mass gap bound is monotonically increasing for `q > 1`.\n\n`Δ_q = E_×(q) · (q − 1)²` where `E_×(q) = (q − q⁻¹)/2`.\nBoth factors are positive and increasing for `q > 1`, so\ntheir product is increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L86-L90","doc":"The mass gap bound vanishes at `q = 1` (classical limit:\nconformal symmetry restored, no mass gap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_pos","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L78-L84","doc":"The mass gap bound is strictly positive for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.massGapBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.massGapBound","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L71-L76","doc":"The **mass gap lower bound** `Δ_q`: the minimum categorical mass\nany non-trivial vortex can have.\n\n`Δ_q = E_×(q) · (q − 1)² = ½(q − q⁻¹)(q − 1)²` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_explicit_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_explicit_pos","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L60-L67","doc":"Explicit formula: at any `q > 1`, the crossing energy\nis `(q² − 1) / (2q)` which is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The minimum crossing energy is strictly positive for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy_eq","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L48-L52","doc":"The minimum crossing energy equals `(q² − 1) / (2q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.minCrossingEnergy","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassGap.lean#L40-L46","doc":"The **minimum crossing energy** (Skein weight) at substrate\nparameter `q`.  Each crossing in a braid word contributes at\nleast this much energy.\n\n`E_×(q) = ½(q − q⁻¹)` ","signatureChunk":0}]}